      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Intussusception occurs when a proximal bowel segment telescopes into a contiguous distal portion. This report describes a rare case of idiopathic intussusception in a 48-year-old female, complaining of right-sided abdominal pain. The abdominal CT scan presents a classic target lesion, representing the cross-sectional image of the intussusceptum layers inside the outer intussuscipiens."},
